title A broken path reds, a narrowed glob goes green
prompt The baton, unattended lap 4089 on grain-grass. Rota row 4 by count, which is Earth.
think Earth is the concrete row, and its instruction is exact: read the fact at the door before any argument about it -- the stamp off a filename, the room token off a Status line, the mark off a value's face. Two of its own three documents are about doors. So I read the door.
think The Earth threshold page names no room in its own Status line. That is a fact at a door, and it sent me to the guard whose whole job is to say so: tools/t/two_rooms_doorway.rish, seated 20260705 with TWO_ROOMS.md.
think Its roster was a shell glob -- for f in external-research/*.md active-designing/*.md docs/*.md -- written when all three rooms were flat. active-designing/ has since folded to date/YYYYMMDD/ under the mark law, and a shell asterisk stops at a slash. So the roster returned 216 post-seating pages where the three rooms hold 1,085.
think I proved the mechanism before believing it rather than after. git ls-files 'counsel/*.md' answers 941, every depth; ls active-designing/*.md answers 110 of 1,055. A git pathspec asterisk crosses a slash and a shell glob does not, and those two spellings read alike on the page. That is the whole defect in one measurement.
think Then I checked whether the reach gap had a live population, since a gap with nothing behind it is a tidiness argument. Running the per-file verdict over the 869 unreached pages: 855 would pass, 14 would fail. Excluding yonder/ and archive/ -- which the shell glob never reached either, so pulling them in would widen the subject rather than restore it -- the honest repair population is 607 pages and 3 failures.
think That separation is the part I would most want a reader to check. A fold files a page rather than retiring it, which is exactly why the mark law chose date/ over archive/: date/ claims only when. So reading a date/ shelf restores the elder reach. Reading yonder/ would be a new judgment, and it is Keaton's rather than mine.
obs The guard was RED before I touched it, and nothing knew. It appears nowhere in construction/standing-equipment.kyri, so no roster pass has ever run it. Run by hand it refused at 45 pages, 42 of them inside its own unrepaired reach. That is REDS %360's family -- a refusal nobody receives -- with an actual refusal standing behind it.
obs And it could not say what it found. assert result.ok stood ahead of say result.out, so the one run that mattered printed "scan failed" and swallowed all 45 page names. Three faults in one instrument, each hiding the next: blind by a glob, deaf by no roster, mute by an assert ordering.
obs This is the third firing of the class in this tree, and the second and third are eleven days apart. index_row_bound read the pin alone and passed four days over 87 unheld rows (%381). log_has_a_row watched the flat session-logs room, measured flat_logs=0 after the born-on-shelf law emptied it, and reported ok for nine days -- repaired 20260905, and its own header says the quiet part: same law moved both files, one guard was repointed and one was not. A lantern that fires three times is a loom.
obs So the repair carries the loom rather than only the fix. The scan floors its own reach on a folded page: should a roster ever narrow to the flat room again, the folded count falls to zero and it refuses, where the elder simply reported a smaller clean tree. That leg is planted in the control by putting the elder glob back, and it bites.
obs I held the ratchet at 45 rather than gating at zero, and the reason is structural rather than convenient: three of the 45 are dated testimony on date/ shelves that accrete-never-break keeps exactly as written, so a hard gate could never close, and a gate that can never close is one somebody turns off.
obs The control passed all fourteen legs on its first run, which I did not trust. Putting the elder roster back at the root flips ten of the fourteen to no. That is the difference between a control that is green and a control that is load-bearing, and it took one command to learn.
obs One of my own legs was a test that cannot fail. grep -qv PATTERN answers yes whenever any line fails to match, so readme_excluded could never have read no. That is %503's class arriving one lap later inside the fixture written to prove a different fix -- caught before it shipped, and replaced by a counted reach: the honest tree holds four pages, two more were planted, the reading must still say four.
obs I killed my own cold roster pass partway. I had edited four files while it ran, so its close digest could only report tree_moved, and eight ships contend for four cores -- twenty more minutes of a pass whose verdict was already void is time taken from peers. The settled cold pass runs below instead.
obs Landed by a later lap rather than by this one. This lap died before its commit and the next round open stashed its work; stash_record_scan.sh read the record as unlanded and lap 4091 read it back out. The row booked here as %506 from a local read is %511 on the anointed spine, which spent %506, then %507 through %509, on other defects while this sat in the box across three laps -- the derived spine's own rule, an unshared row renumbers to the fetched head, and it renumbered twice.
