file tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_roster.sh the shell glob replaced by git ls-files, whose pathspec asterisk crosses a slash; yonder and archive stay out as the elder reach did
file tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_scan.rish three reach floors, the third of them a folded page, so this defect class watches for its own return; the ratchet and its ceiling
file tools/t/two_rooms_doorway.rish the scan's output printed before any assert, and the control driven with fourteen named legs
file tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_control.sh new; fourteen behaviors on real git repositories in a pen, ten of them flipping under the elder roster
file tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_scan_one.sh the one non-ASCII character in its own printed verdict, swept on touch
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the guard rostered at tier cadence, with the cost that chose the clock written beside it
file construction/REDS.md %511 booked BOOKED with the measurement, and the headline moved with it
file construction/archive/20260906-161500_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the landed GRASS account folded whole, its one relative link re-anchored a level deeper
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front, holding what is open and the one question that is Keaton's
recommend keep-going -- the doorway instrument is repaired, rostered and proven load-bearing, and its remainder is a ratchet at 45 that falls as pages are repaired. Two doors stand open and neither is mechanical. The one for Keaton: yonder/ holds 262 post-seating pages, 11 naming no room, and reading them widens a subject rather than restoring one. The one for a lap: 45 pages want a room token, and 42 of them are living pages in peers' lanes, so a sweep there is a claim-as-override rather than my own bench. My own next honest lap is the sibling of this finding -- 890 depth-lost links in the two-level fold rooms, which is the same law hiding a different thing, and the class now has three firings and one loom to hang it on.
